              "date": "2026-11-13T23:09:19Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch fixes a bug in the Btrfs file system where data space is released twice when a direct IO COW write fails, leading to an underflow of bytes_may_use and potential warnings or clamping to zero. The fix involves recording the extent consumed by btrfs_reserve_extent() in dio_data and releasing only the remaining reserved data space from bytes_may_use on error paths. This patch can be applied to stable kernels later than v5.19, which rewrote the affected error path.",
